            <ArticleTitle>[Prader-Willi syndrome].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>20-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Prader-Willi syndrome is a rare genetic disease that affects neurodevelopment in children. It is characterised by major behavioural problems and morbid obesity. Early diagnosis and growth hormone treatment can bring out considerable improvements. However, the outlook for adults remains problematic.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
